dism (E11)", "Muscle biopsy referenced but lacking text-characterised findings (Figure A) (E23)", "Systemic symptoms: depression, weight gain, fatigue consistent with metabolic/endocrine pathology (E3-E4)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Electrolyte disturbance alone: Hypokalemia without biopsy confirmation cannot anchor root node as primary mechanism (lower posterior in B4)", "Hypoglycemic complication: Glucose 70 mg/dL (mild hypoglycemia) insufficient to explain chronic progressive weakness (B4 evidence against)", "Antibiotic-induced allergy with secondary myopathy: Requires biopsy correlation for systemic mechanism validation (B1 evidence against)", "Diabetic polyneuropathy: Unlikely mechanism given recent onset with 2/5 symmetric strength despite absence of sensory deficits (B3 evidence against)"], "alarm_features": ["Mild fever (37.5°C) (E9)", "Multiple hypoglycemic admissions (E8)", "New-onset rash temporally linked to recent antibiotic use (E12)(E6)", "Unexplained weight gain and depression (E3-E4)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Inflammatory Myopathy", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.3, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Endocrine/Metabolic Myopathy", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3, "posterior": 0.3, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any history of thyroid dysfunction? (weight gain, cold intolerance)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["TSH and free T4 testing>", "Serum electrolytes with correction for metabolic causes>"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Other Neuromuscular Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.05, "posterior": 0.05, "danger": 0.1, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any recent viral illnesses? (rhabdomyolysis/acute myopathy)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Repeat MRI to evaluate for fatty replacement>", "Muscle biopsy immunostains (per Figure A)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.2, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "other"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Degenerative/Idiopathic Myopathy", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is the weakness asymmetric with distal involvement?", "Any family history of similar muscle disease? (inflammatory vs degenerative patterns)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Genetic testing for limb-girdle muscular dystrophy>", "Muscle biopsy for amyloid or inclusion bodies (see Figure A)>"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 4.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Secondary Hypokalemic Myopathy", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.25, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B2", "B3", "B5", "B1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the age of onset (57) and subacute progression (6 months) with asymmetric symptoms make inclusion body myositis more likely than other degenerative myopathies?", "result_summary": "Age over 50 with subacute asymmetric weakness moderately increases inclusion body myositis likelihood compared to other degenerative etiologies (e.g., polymyositis), which typically have symmetric patterns.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "moderate_for", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the documented hypokalemia (3.3 mEq/L) and recent streptococcal antibiotic use correlate with a drug-induced secondary hypokalemic state?", "result_summary": "The hypokalemia without gastrointestinal losses or diuretic use weakens direct drug-induced hypokalemia, though streptococcal infections can cause rashes, complicating the temporal linkage.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "weak_for"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the normal AST/ALT levels (E21-E22) inconsistent with inflammatory myopathy as the primary explanation?", "result_summary": "Normal muscle enzymes strongly contradict an inflammatory myopathy, as these typically show significant elevations in disease activity.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "strong_against", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absence of classic hypothyroid symptoms (cold intolerance, constipation) inconsistent with endocrine/metabolic myopathy as a primary diagnosis?", "result_summary": "The absence of prototypical hypothyroid features (e.g., cold intolerance) diminishes support for endocrine/metabolic causes despite secondary signs (hair loss).", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 6, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the reported physical findings (2/5 strength, rash) inconsistent with typical features of inclusion body myositis?", "result_summary": "Facial/upper extremity rashes are not typical of inclusion body myositis, slightly reducing its likelihood compared to purely degenerative mechanisms.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "moderate_against", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 7, "bundle_size": 8, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the systemic manifestations (depression, weight gain) without gastrointestinal losses incompatible with a primary hypokalemic myopathy?", "result_summary": "Weight gain and depression lack mechanistic linkage to potassium imbalance, making a primary hypokalemic cause less probable.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "moderate_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.15921423859270437, "B2": 0.2899660692815884, "B3": 0.35103468084240785, "B4": 0.08277345100249701, "B5": 0.1170115602808026, "B3.1": 0.21062080850544468, "B3.2": 0.10531040425272234, "B3.3": 0.03510346808424078}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B3) has posterior=0.35 without meeting confirmation threshold (>0.75). Dangerous inflammatory myopathy branch (B1) has posterior=0.16 with danger=0.6, but neither exceeds exclusion boundary (posterior<0.